      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none font-mono leading-relaxed">

<p class="mb-4">"Best matcha in Sant Feliu" is an honest search, but let's be straightforward: the competition for ceremonial matcha in Sant Feliu de Guíxols isn't particularly high. Most places have something on the menu. Not all of them care about where it comes from.</p>
<p class="mb-4">If the question is where to get a matcha latte made with traceable Japanese tea, the nearest answer is five minutes away: Dirty Rabbit in S'Agaró.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What makes a good matcha latte</h3>
<ol class="list-decimal list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>Where the tea comes from. Japanese ceremonial matcha has its own flavour — without the bitterness of generic powder. At Dirty Rabbit we use REQ Matcha, a Barcelona project founded by a Japanese man who lives in Japan and selects the tea directly at the plantations.</li>
  <li>The dose. We serve 2g of ceremonial matcha per cup — enough to be recognisable without being heavy. There's an extra strong option for a little more if you want more body.</li>
  <li>Preparation temperature. Matcha doesn't mix well when dissolved directly into hot milk. We whisk it with cold water first. Small step, big impact on texture and flavour.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">What matcha you can order</h3>
<ul class="list-disc list-outside ml-6 space-y-2 mb-6">
  <li>Classic matcha latte — hot or iced, with plant milk available</li>
  <li>Orange matcha — with orange juice instead of milk (dairy-free, more refreshing)</li>
  <li>Extra strong — higher dose, for a little more</li>
</ul>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Where to find the best matcha near Sant Feliu de Guíxols</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Dirty Rabbit, Avinguda Platja d'Aro 275, S'Agaró. Five minutes from Sant Feliu along the GI-682.</p>
<p class="mb-4">We opened on 1 November 2024. Iwonka runs the place with a simple logic: every ingredient on the menu has a name and an origin. Matcha from REQ Matcha. Coffee from La Cabra. Bread from Origo Bakery. Nothing anonymous.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Large terrace, WiFi, and good natural light in the mornings. Coming from Sant Feliu, take the GI-682 towards Platja d'Aro — we're before you reach the S'Agaró residential area.</p>
<h3 class="font-typewriter text-xl mb-4 mt-8">Why matcha is everywhere but good matcha is rare</h3>
<p class="mb-4">Quality matcha costs money. Japanese ceremonial-grade powder is in a different price bracket from generic imports, and that affects what most places actually buy. Adding "matcha latte" to a menu is easy. Working with the right supplier is a different decision.</p>
<p class="mb-4">This conversation arrived late to the Costa Brava. The places doing matcha well are the same ones doing coffee well — it's the same philosophy applied to a different ingredient. There are few in the area, but they're here.</p>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
