</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">How much does a matcha latte cost at Dirty Rabbit?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Between €3.50 and €5. The price reflects the ingredient cost.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Is it suitable for people who are lactose intolerant?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes. We serve the matcha latte with plant-based options. Ask at the counter what we have that day.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-black/10 pb-5">
  <p class="font-typewriter font-bold mb-2">Are you open in the mornings?</p>
  <p class="font-mono text-sm text-black/70 leading-relaxed">Yes. Good natural morning light is one of the things the space is known for. Check current hours on our social media or call +34 872 454 264.</p>
</div>
<hr class="my-8 border-black/20" />
</div>
<h2 class="font-typewriter text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6 mt-12">About Dirty Rabbit</h2>
<p class="mb-4">We opened on 1 November 2024 in S'Agaró. Specialty coffee, properly made alternative drinks, and a place to stay in if you want.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Iwonka runs day-to-day with a clear rule on suppliers: if she can't explain where an ingredient comes from, it doesn't go on the menu. Matcha from REQ Matcha. Coffee from La Cabra. Bread from Origo Bakery.</p>
<p class="mb-4">Natural light in the mornings, WiFi, large terrace when the weather holds. The kind of place where you can work through a morning without anyone minding.</p>

